A||||1||btoth||Mac OS X question||||5||
Z||000000||btoth||10-07-2001||11:29 PM||||I know that OS X is basically BSD Unix with the cool GUI.  (Obviously it's more than that, but I'm simpliflying.)  I've read that it can run UNIX progams - things like apache, and other programs.  Do any of you that use it know if any one the Unix Windows emulators can run under it as well??||||reg||5
Z||000001||beer_stud_21||10-08-2001||04:12 PM||||OS X is basically FreeBSD+NeXTSTEP+Apple Designed GUI (called "Aqua")  Its obviously not that simple, but basically thats what OS X is made out of.  OS X can run unix programs.  Not everything, but quite a bit of stuff.  I know a lot (all?) of the terminal programs run in X.  I'm 99% sure none of the windows emulators wouldnt run.  Especially since they would normally would be running on x86 hardware where when running on OS X would be running on PowerPC.  If you want to emulate windows on OS X you need Virtual PC Test Drive for Mac OS X.  Its free if you have VPC 4.  BTW:  Apache is installed by default in Mac OS X <P>-Marlin||||reg||1
